. Explanation for your report
Why is a normal Queue insufficient?
A normal FIFO Queue serves patients in arrival order only. It cannot automatically serve the most severe patient first.
How does PriorityQueue work?
Severity 1 has the highest priority.
Severity 5 has the lowest priority.
If two patients have equal severity, the arrival counter serves the earlier patient first.
poll() removes and returns the highest-priority patient.
Why use an arrival counter?
The counter gives every patient a unique arrival number. It preserves arrival order when severity levels are equal.
